# Suggested Hooks — fastapi

## Stack Summary

| Tool | Version / Source | Config Location |
|------|-----------------|-----------------|
| Ruff (lint + format) | `>=0.14.14` (dev dep) | `[tool.ruff.*]` in `pyproject.toml` |
| mypy | `>=1.14.1` (dev dep), strict mode | `[tool.mypy]` in `pyproject.toml` |
| ty | `>=0.0.9` (dev dep) | n/a (no config section) |
| pytest | `>=9.0.0` with xdist, timeout=20s | `[tool.pytest]` in `pyproject.toml` |
| pre-commit | ruff, mypy, ty hooks via `uv run` | `.pre-commit-config.yaml` |

---

## Hook 1 — Ruff Lint Auto-Fix

Automatically fixes lint issues when Python files are written or edited.

FastAPI's ruff config selects rules E, W, F, I (isort), B (bugbear), C4 (comprehensions), and UP (pyupgrade), with intentional ignores for E501 (line length), B008 (function calls in defaults — core FastAPI pattern), C901 (complexity), and W191 (tabs). Extensive per-file ignores exist for `docs_src/` tutorial files. Running ruff automatically prevents import ordering, unused imports, and style issues from accumulating between commits.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "ruff check --fix \"$FILE_PATH\"",
        "description": "Auto-fix lint issues with ruff (E/W/F/I/B/C4/UP rules)"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: `pip install ruff` or `uv sync` (already in `docs-tests` dependency group: `ruff >=0.14.14`)

