## Hook 2 — Ruff Format Check

Checks formatting on written Python files and reports deviations without auto-fixing, so you see the diff before committing.

FastAPI runs `ruff format` across `fastapi/`, `tests/`, `docs_src/`, and `scripts/`. The pre-commit hook uses `--exit-non-zero-on-format` to block malformatted commits. A post-write check catches formatting drift immediately rather than at commit time.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "ruff format --check --diff \"$FILE_PATH\"",
        "description": "Check ruff formatting on changed Python files"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: Same `ruff` install as above. To auto-format instead of just checking, replace `--check --diff` with just the file path: `ruff format "$FILE_PATH"`.

