## Hook 4 — Pytest for Modified Test Files

Runs the specific test file when a test file is modified, with the required `PYTHONPATH` set.

FastAPI's test suite requires `PYTHONPATH=./docs_src` because tests import tutorial examples from `docs_src/` as modules. Tests have a 20-second timeout and run with `pytest-xdist`. This hook runs only the changed test file (not the full suite) to keep feedback under a few seconds.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "if echo \"$FILE_PATH\" | grep -qE '^tests/.*\\.py$'; then PYTHONPATH=./docs_src pytest \"$FILE_PATH\" -x --timeout=20 --no-header -q 2>&1 | tail -20; fi",
        "description": "Run modified test file with PYTHONPATH=./docs_src"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: `pip install pytest pytest-timeout` (already in `tests` dependency group). Also install test dependencies: `uv sync` or `pip install -e ".[all]"` plus the test extras.

