## Hook 5 — Large File Warning

Warns when a file exceeds 500 lines, which helps catch overgrown modules.

FastAPI's core source files are deliberately compact — most are under 300 lines. The largest (`routing.py`, `dependencies/utils.py`) are around 800–1000 lines and are already considered complex. A 500-line threshold flags when a file is growing beyond the norm for this codebase, prompting a refactoring conversation before it becomes unwieldy.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "LINE_COUNT=$(wc -l < \"$FILE_PATH\"); if [ \"$LINE_COUNT\" -gt 500 ]; then echo \"⚠️  Warning: $FILE_PATH is $LINE_COUNT lines (threshold: 500)\"; fi",
        "description": "Warn if file exceeds 500 lines"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: No additional tools needed — uses standard shell commands.

