## Hooks NOT Suggested (and Why)

| Tool | Why Excluded |
|------|-------------|
| **ty** (type checker) | The repo uses `ty check fastapi` in pre-commit and lint scripts, but `ty` is a very new tool (v0.0.9) with rapidly changing behavior. Running it as a post-write hook would likely produce noisy, unstable output. Better left for pre-commit or manual runs until it stabilizes. |
| **Black** | Not used for formatting — the repo uses `ruff format`. Black is only a docs dependency for code rendering in MkDocs. |
| **ESLint / TypeScript** | Not applicable — this is a pure Python project. |
| **Coverage** | `pytest-cov` is installed but coverage is a full-suite metric, not useful as a per-file post-write hook. |
| **pre-commit run** | The `.pre-commit-config.yaml` includes doc-related hooks (permalinks, README generation, translation fixes) that are expensive and irrelevant during development. The individual tool hooks above are faster and more targeted. |
